DATA = 'Newton second law|F=m*a|F,m,a|s+s|F is NET force along selected axis.|P:1,-a*m;P:-a,F;P:-m,F\nKinetic friction|F=mu*N|F,mu,N|s00|Magnitude; direction opposes slipping.|P:1,-N*mu;P:-N,F;P:-mu,F\nStatic friction limit|F=mu*N|F,mu,N|s00|MAXIMUM static friction, not actual friction.|P:1,-N*mu;P:-N,F;P:-mu,F\nSpring force|F=-ks*x|F,ks,x|s+s|x measured from spring equilibrium.|P:1,ks*x;P:x,F;P:ks,F\nGravity force|F=G*M*m/r^2|F,M,m,r|s+++|Magnitude; point masses or external spheres.|P:r^2,-G*M*m;P:-G*m,F*r^2;P:-G*M,F*r^2;P:F,0,-G*M*m\nCircular acceleration|a=v^2/r|a,v,r|ss+|Radial magnitude; inward direction.|P:r,-v^2;P:-1,0,a*r;P:a,-v^2\nCentripetal net force|F=m*v^2/r|F,m,v,r|s+s+|NET radial force; not an additional force.|P:r,-m*v^2;P:-v^2,F*r;P:-m,0,F*r;P:F,-m*v^2\nIncline gravity|F=m*g*sin(th)|F,m,th|s+s|Component downhill; g=9.8.|P:1,-g*m*sin(th);P:-g*sin(th),F;E:\nIncline normal|N=m*g*cos(th)|N,m,th|0+s|No other perpendicular forces; g=9.8.|P:1,-g*m*cos(th);P:-g*cos(th),N;E:\nIdeal banked turn|v^2=r*g*tan(th)|v,r,th|s+s|No friction; angle from horizontal.|P:1,0,-g*r*tan(th);P:-g*tan(th),v^2;E:\nLinear drag terminal|v=m*g/b|v,m,b|s++|Downward terminal speed; drag=-b*v.|P:b,-g*m;P:-g,b*v;P:v,-g*m\nFall with linear drag|v=m*g/b*(1-exp(-b*t/m))|v,m,b,t|s++0|Starts at rest; positive downward; g=9.8.|P:b*exp(b*t/m),-g*m*exp(b*t/m) + g*m;E:;E:;E:m*ln(-g*m/(b*v - g*m))/b\nOrbital speed|v^2=G*M/r|v,M,r|s++|Circular orbit; r from source center.|P:r,0,-G*M;P:-G,r*v^2;P:v^2,-G*M\nOrbit period|T^2=4*pi^2*r^3/(G*M)|T,r,M|0++|Circular orbit; negligible orbiting mass.|P:G*M,0,-4*pi^2*r^3;E:(1/2)*2^(1/3)*G^(1/3)*M^(1/3)*abs(T)^(2/3)/pi^(2/3);P:G*T^2,-4*pi^2*r^3'
